[E0319] Error: `Event` carries values, so it is not a number
    ╭─[ err/151_enum_numbers/main.wip:14:13 ]
    │
 14 │     val n = Event::Quit as i64
    │             ─────────┬────────  
    │                      ╰────────── not an enum of names alone
    │ 
    │ Note: an enum whose variants carry nothing is which one it holds, and one that carries values is that and what it holds
────╯
[E0319] Error: cannot convert `Colour` to `f64`
    ╭─[ err/151_enum_numbers/main.wip:15:13 ]
    │
 15 │     val f = Colour::Red as f64
    │             ─────────┬────────  
    │                      ╰────────── not a numeric conversion
    │ 
    │ Note: `as` converts between the integer types, `f32` and `f64`, between C pointer types, and between a pointer and an integer as wide as one, `usize`, `isize`, `u64` or `i64`
────╯
[E0319] Error: cannot convert `i64` to `Colour`
    ╭─[ err/151_enum_numbers/main.wip:16:13 ]
    │
 16 │     val c = 1 as Colour
    │             ─────┬─────  
    │                  ╰─────── not a numeric conversion
    │ 
    │ Help: `Colour::fromIndex(n)` answers the variant with that number, or nothing where `Colour` has no such variant
    │ 
    │ Note: `as` converts between the integer types, `f32` and `f64`, between C pointer types, and between a pointer and an integer as wide as one, `usize`, `isize`, `u64` or `i64`
────╯
